// REJECTS: Unsupported persistence target type 'Snowflake'
//
// The second island on a Persistence element: the right-hand side of `serviceOutput ->
// target`. `targetSpecification: targetType (targetValue)?` with `targetType: identifier`,
// so any name followed by any `#{ ... }#` body parses; the name selects a registered
// PersistenceTarget processor, and `Relational` is the only one shipped.
//
// Note what this means for the island BODY: the text between `#{` and `}#` is never lexed
// unless a processor claims the type. The body below is deliberately nonsense, and the error
// is still about the TYPE -- which is how you tell a missing grammar extension on the
// classpath (README: "Unsupported Data Source Specification type") apart from a genuine
// grammar limit.
###Persistence
Persistence test::persistence::neg::InventedTarget
{
  doc: 'a persistence target type nobody registered';
  trigger: Manual;
  service: test::persistence::Service;
  serviceOutputTargets:
  [
    TDS
    {
      keys:
      [
        foo
      ]
      datasetType: Delta
      {
        actionIndicator: None;
      }
    }
    ->
    Snowflake
    #{
      not: even; close: to; a: grammar;
    }#
  ];
}
